189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (What is a Database?)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Before learning Prisma deeply, let us understand what a database actually is. If you already know this, feel free to skip ahead.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (A Database is Like a Spreadsheet)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Imagine a Google Sheet with tabs. Each tab is a 'table'. Each row is a record \(like one user\). Each column is a field \(like name, email, age\). A database is basically a super-powered spreadsheet that can handle millions of rows and multiple apps reading/writing at once.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Why Not Just Use a Spreadsheet?)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Spreadsheets break with lots of data, have no rules to prevent bad data, and cannot handle thousands of users at once. Databases are built for speed, security, and reliability. They enforce rules like 'email must be unique' automatically.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (SQL: The Language of Databases)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (SQL \(Structured Query Language\) is how you talk to a database. Commands like SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE tell the database what to do. Prisma writes this SQL for you, so you do not need to learn it right away.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Where Prisma Fits In)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
198 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Your app \(JavaScript/TypeScript\) cannot talk to a database directly in a friendly way. Prisma sits in between. You write simple JavaScript, Prisma converts it to SQL, sends it to the database, and gives you back clean results.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
